    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 `telephone` for humans, keeping the raw `telephone` as E.164.\n\nThree files touched, each change small and self-contained:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the derived, read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the getter/setter.\n\n2. **`TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new) \u2014 a tiny helper mirroring the existing `E164Telephone`/`IdentityKey` pattern (single static `of`, no surrounding class complexity). It splits off the country code (leading `61`, else a single digit \u2014 matching what `E164Telephone` produces) and groups the national digits in threes: `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one extra `@Mapping` expression delegating to `TelephoneDisplay.of(owner.getTelephone())`, consistent with the other derived-field mappings.\n\nNo existing method grew \u2014 the derivation lives in its own cohesive unit rather than expanding the mapper or any large class. The `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` acceptance test and the full suite pass.",
